	(text "NIBBLE CARD MEMCTL - DATA MEMORY CONTROL: the address register and the write and read gates for the slot cards"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d3ebed60-a7d8-4451-83b8-6529b6bbb1bc")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  59 transistors, 39 resistors, 4 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: BUS3#..BUS0# (an address while MAI), MAI, MI, MO, CLK.\nTo the slot cards over the LINK ribbon (2x6, chained along the eight slot cards): MAR3..0 and their complements, MIN (low = write allowed: MI and PH1), MON (low = read: MO).\nMAR is four transparent latches open while MAI and PH1 (the address rides the bus for the whole tick).  The write ends at the clock edge because PH1 does (D0xx: a write that\noutlasted the data flipped cells at the mixed corner).  Each slot card selects its pair of slots from MAR3..1 with jumpers and its even/odd slot with MAR0."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1b15df74-2ddb-4df8-8514-a665f0b029dd")
	)
	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK: only PH1 is used here, to close the address latches and end the write before the rising edge"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5fd9389a-3bd3-4653-b409-db617696b873")
	)
